>dead that I was carrying a +3 elven dagger or something.
>What other ways are there of finding out what things are?  I always get to
>about level 10 carrying about loads of stuff and leaving piles in corners
>and chests waiting to find a scroll of identify, and then get killed by
>something I probably had the means to defeat.

Spoilers follow.



You're better off piling your stuff up in shops.  The shopkeeper will
tell you that's a +3 dagger about as fast as an altar will tell you
that it's blessed.  And he'll tell you the level of spellbooks that
you leave in his care.  He'll give you useful information about
scrolls (especially identify), potions, armor, and rings, too.  Of
course, you have to understand the shopkeeper's language, which is
money.  Some of the information contained in the WCST spoiler may be
useful here.

Unfortunately, the shopkeeper will not help you identify amulets.  The
WCST spoilers include some clever tricks though.

